This derivative modifies the original. Notable changes:
  - Add the steps before the code: check the spec is complete, read the glossary and the
    decision record, start the version when the release branch is missing, and cut the
    work branch, stacked on a dependency when the spec names one.
  - Add the steps after the code: the commit and the PR through sibling skills.
  - Add three checkpoints at which the user reads the tests, the code, and the review.
  - Name a sibling skill for every step instead of the original's tdd and code-review.
  - Make the skill model-invocable with a narrow description so that the spec planner
    can load it.

The core — one piece of work from a spec, tests first at pre-agreed seams, typecheck and
single test files as you go with the full suite once at the end, a review, then a commit —
is carried from the original.
